{"type":"standard","title":"Josh Shapiro","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Josh Shapiro</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q6289368","titles":{"canonical":"Josh_Shapiro","normalized":"Josh Shapiro","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Josh Shapiro</span></span>"},"pageid":15624731,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Gov._Shapiro.jpg/330px-Gov._Shapiro.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":489},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/02/Gov._Shapiro.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":899,"height":1332},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1374358833","tid":"77de2877-adf0-11f1-828f-31bbabcb90c4","timestamp":"2026-09-11T14:52:54Z","description":"Governor of Pennsylvania since 2023","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Josh_Shapiro","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Josh_Shapiro?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Josh_Shapiro?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Josh_Shapiro"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Josh_Shapiro","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Josh_Shapiro","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Josh_Shapiro?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Josh_Shapiro"}},"extract":"Joshua David Shapiro is an American politician and lawyer serving since 2023 as the 48th governor of Pennsylvania. A member of the Democratic Party, he was the attorney general of Pennsylvania from 2017 to 2023 and served on the Montgomery County Board of Commissioners from 2012 to 2017.","extract_html":"<p><b>Joshua David Shapiro</b> is an American politician and lawyer serving since 2023 as the 48th governor of Pennsylvania. A member of the Democratic Party, he was the attorney general of Pennsylvania from 2017 to 2023 and served on the Montgomery County Board of Commissioners from 2012 to 2017.</p>"}